CLEAN-ROOM STATEMENT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

tethermesh is an independent implementation. It contains no code derived from
the Meshtastic firmware, its mobile or desktop clients, its protobuf schemas, or
from RadioLib.

The Meshtastic firmware, clients and schemas are GPL-3.0, and nothing here is
derived from them. RadioLib is MIT, NOT GPL-3.0 -- this file said otherwise
until 2026-08-20, which was simply wrong about somebody else's project. It may
be read for facts, on the same footing as any other second implementation, and
nothing here is derived from it either. Non-derivation is a statement about
expression and is not enforced by any script: matching a project's name would
have proved something about vocabulary and nothing about code.

Protocol facts were established from published documentation, from the schemas
read as specification, and from black-box observation of a pinned reference
build and of real on-air traffic. tools/check_cleanroom.sh enforces the GPL
boundary on every run, over the working tree and over vendored submodules.

